The YASD risks may be only incrementally higher.  But the risk to just 
die, *not* die by stupidity (except if you consider doing the racket 
itself as a stupidity) will probably be quite a lot higher.  It is 
different to be hit at 12 or 14 Hp than to be hit at 50 Hp.  And there 
is no way to avoid being hit when your pet is eating and you don't have 
the speed to run away from those three gnomes that are after you.

I think this is a question that could in principle be answered 
objectively.  Let 100 players run 10 games each, 5 of them with and 5 
without the protection racket.  I am pretty sure that those without the 
racket will advance further on average.  Of course, you can have the 
same thing done by experts on the racket; I would still bet that except 
possibly for the healer (and maybe the tourist), non-racket games will 
have a higer survival rate.

This is not a judgement on fun, of course.  If you have more fun doing 
it and don't might the higher rate of losses, just do it.
